{"id": "BG-FID-008", "packet": "loop\\packets\\BG-FID-008.md", "slot": 2, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "verdict": "REJECTED", "verify_verdict": "ACCEPTED", "adjudication": "orchestrator soundness review: rejected despite every gate PASS. (A) disc-membership inclusion decided by box_distance (INFIMUM distance) <= eps proves the root box INTERSECTS the ball, not that the certified root lies in it: a coverage-violation crossing at eps + 2e-5 inside a width-1e-4 decision box certifies Ok(ExactlyOne) with true count 0. (B) the narrow stop (DISC_DECIDE_WIDTH) counts 1 and discards the box after Krawczyk Unique, but NUM-003 krawczyk returns on the first internal sub-box proof and does not enumerate the query box, so a second crossing within 1e-4 of parameter is lost -> false ExactlyOne. Both are packet-text defects the worker diagnosed in disagreements #2/#3; amended by BG-FID-008-r2.", "gates": {"V0": "PASS", "V1": "PASS", "V10": "SKIP", "V2": "PASS", "V3": "PASS", "V4": "PASS", "V5": "PASS", "V6": "PASS", "V7": "PASS", "V8": "PASS", "V9": "PASS"}, "worker_commit": "c6a833e", "branch": "packet/BG-FID-008", "timestamp": "2026-08-23T01:35:20.524532Z", "fault": "PACKET", "fault_note": "step-4 parenthetical conflated box-intersects-ball with whole-box-inside-ball (inf vs sup distance), and Decision 1 stated KrawczykProof::Unique means one root in the query box, which the shipped NUM-003 operator does not guarantee"}
